                <pb facs="0399" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg301"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herdliska to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 118.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    this morning of Acting Secretary Adee’s open telegram of yesterday’s date,
                    reading as follows:<anchor n="1" xml:id="d346-f1"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Immediately upon receipt of the above cablegram I called upon Count Szecsen, in
                    the absence of Count Goluchowski on leave. Imperial and royal acting minister
                    for foreign affairs, and communicated the contents thereof to him, handing him
                    at the same time a copy. Count Szecsen expressed his thanks for the
                    communication and assured me that the information imparted and the attitude
                    taken by the United States would be received with great satisfaction by the
                    Imperial and Royal Government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles V. Herdliska</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
